/-!
# A cusp retraction with a prescribed honeycomb endpoint

The explicit tent cutoff in genuine positive logarithmic coordinates
modifies the previously constructed deformation at one chosen positive
height. Concatenation, actual compact-torus phase spreading, the explicit
frozen straightening, and actual quotient descent give an unconditional
strong deformation retraction of every sufficiently small closed cusp
neighborhood. Its restriction to the chosen literal nonzero fibre is
exactly the independently defined honeycomb collapse.

Central points are fixed throughout, the base norm does not increase,
and the toric homotopy is equivariant for the actual lattice and compact
fibre-torus actions. The small neighborhood radius is chosen before the
fibre, and the controlled homotopy after it. No deformation of the entire
open tube or simultaneous prescription at all levels is asserted.
-/
